      "id": "88213038-202d-4554-bdaf-eceda4f590cc",
      "body": "Facts for the planner of task `t-review-check`, read 2026-11-27T09:57Z, and two decisions of this issue's architect.\n\n- **#5700's head moved.** cybermonklabs/legion#5700 (ACME-3223, branch `legion/ACME-3223`) is open at head `d76c2a50375482cf5b8dbfa1280320f9246a70f1`, base `main`, merge state `BLOCKED`. Its `packages/daemon/internal/prompts/roles/reviewer.md` is 1,394 bytes at that head, not the 1,251 bytes at `4962fc95c5` that the spec's Design names; `main`'s is 13,179 bytes and goes away with #5700. Plan the reviewer text against the head the implementer merges forward.\n- **No step runs in the harness.** At `d76c2a5037`, `packages/pi-legion/scripts/skill-scenarios/heldout-case.ts` takes `set: devcase`, and neither it nor `daemon-standin.ts` holds step runs. So the step runs that R1's test reads are part of this task, in the world and in the stand-in.\n- **Decision: tell ACME-3223 the lines first.** Before its first push that changes a file #5700 changes, the implementer writes a Dispatch comment on dispatch://ACME-3223 with `--mention-role legion-acme-acme-3223-architect` that names each file and the exact lines the change touches. ACME-3223's architect asked for this, and the deployment's rule for a change that touches another open pull request's files says the same. It does not wait for an answer.\n- **Decision: no children.** This issue is one pull request in cybermonklabs/legion. The reviewer text and the harness step runs are proven by one case, so a split would only run them in sequence.\n",
